    "evidence_text": "The factors that determine the stimulatory potency of a pMHC molecule remain unclear.\n\nThis conclusion was supported by experiments that showed that enhancing cSMAC formation reduced stimulatory capacity of the weak peptide.\n\nTCR ligand density and affinity determine peripheral induction of Foxp3 in vivo\n\nThis occurs earlier than and independently of tyrosine kinase activation.\n\nT cell receptor ligation induces the formation of dynamically regulated signaling assemblies\n\nDirect observation of ligand recognition by T cells\n\nIncreased sensitivity of antigen-experienced T cells through the enrichment of oligomeric T cell receptor complexes.\n\nOur studies reveal a role for F-actin in TCR signaling beyond microcluster formation.\n\nMechanical modulation of receptor-ligand interactions at cell-cell interfaces.\n\nWe find robust supradiffusive segregation of LSMs from a single receptor-ligand complex.\n\nNo studies have been published on naive T cell IS dynamics.\n\nHere, we find that IS formation during antigen recognition comprises cycles of stable IS formation and autonomous naive T cell migration.\n\nThus, opposing effects of PKCtheta and WASp control IS stability through pSMAC symmetry breaking and reformation.\n\nAltered TCR signaling from geometrically repatterned immunological synapses.",
